
---
import DocsLayout from '/src/layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import DocsCode from '/src/components/DocsCode.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Lua & LSL Docs">
<div class="dashboard summary-function">
  <div class="dashboard-header">
    <span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`ll.IntegerToBase64(Value: number): string`} lang="slua" /></span>
    <span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`string llIntegerToBase64(integer Value);`} lang="lsl" /></span>
  </div>

  <div class="dashboard-body">
    <div class="dash-col">
      <p>  <p>Returns a string that is a <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Category:LSL_Base64" target="_blank">Base64</a> big endian encode of <b>number</b></p>
</p>
      <table class="param-table" id="parameters">
        <tr>
          <td><span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span>number</span></td>
          <td><span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span>integer</span></td>
          <td>Value / <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Category:LSL_Parameters/number" target="_blank">number</a></td>
          <td></td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="dash-col">
      <div class="dash-section-title">Categories</div>
      <ul class="meta-list">
        <li>data_conversion</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="dash-col">
      <div class="dash-section-title">Tech Specs</div>
      <div class="tech-item"><span class="tech-label">Energy</span><span class="tech-val">10</span></div>
      <div class="tech-item"><span class="tech-label">LSO ID</span><span class="tech-val">280</span></div>

      <div class="label-stack">
        <span class="attr-label bg-pure">Side-Effect Free</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
  <h2>Examples</h2>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`local function ASCII7ToString(letter)
    if letter >= 0x80 or letter < 0 then  --Not valid ascii7 character
        return ""
    end
    return ll.Base64ToString(ll.IntegerToBase64(bit32.lshift(letter, 24)))
end
`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`string ASCII7ToString(integer letter)
{
    if(letter >= 0x80 || letter < 0) return "";//Not valid ascii7 character
    return llBase64ToString(llIntegerToBase64(letter << 24));
}`} lang="lsl" /></div>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`ll = llcompat

-- Packs a 24-bit unsigned integer value (0-16777215) to only 4 Base64 characters.
local function Int24ToBase64(value)
    return ll.GetSubString(ll.IntegerToBase64(bit32.lshift(value, 8)), 0, 3)
end
-- unpacks a 4-character Base64 value to a 24-bit unsigned integer
local function Base64ToInt24(value)
    return bit32.band(bit32.arshift(ll.Base64ToInteger(value), 8), 0xffffff)  -- Masking required to remove sign extension from bit-shifting
end
`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`// Packs a 24-bit unsigned integer value (0-16777215) to only 4 Base64 characters.
string Int24ToBase64(integer value)
{
    return llGetSubString(llIntegerToBase64(value<<8), 0, 3);
}
// unpacks a 4-character Base64 value to a 24-bit unsigned integer
integer Base64ToInt24(string value)
{
    return (llBase64ToInteger(value)>>8)&0xffffff; // Masking required to remove sign extension from bit-shifting
}`} lang="lsl" /></div>
  <p>If you are looking for full Unicode translation, not just ASCII7 see: <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Combined_Library#Unicode_Integer_to_UTF8" target="_blank">Combined_Library</a></p>
  <h2>Notes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Only the first 6 of the 8 characters returned are needed to decoded it back into an integer. The padding "==" can be safely removed for storage.</li>
    <li>"Big-endian" refers to the fact that the most significant, i.e. highest byte of the integer is processed first: the first characters in the returned Base64 string correspond to this byte, and the last characters correspond to the least significant byte.
    <ul>
      <li>Combined with bit-shifting, removing characters from the Base64 string allows more efficient packing of small values. See <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlBase64ToInteger#Caveats" target="_blank">llBase64ToInteger caveats</a> for specifics.</li>
    </ul>
  
    </li>
  </ul>
